  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#15653\"], \"answer\": \"This looks like a known limitation rather than something specific to your setup. Windows Terminal doesn't give screen readers (NVDA, Narrator, JAWS) a reliable way to tell which option is selected in an interactive CLI prompt. The screen reader reads terminal output instead of the selected item, so it can announce the wrong option. The maintainers said there is no robust fix yet, that work on it started in #14342 and is progressing slowly, and that the issue is tracked in #13666. There is no workaround in the archived tickets. Add your repro (Copilot CLI, Up Arrow onto the first option announces the second) to #13666 and follow it for updates.\"}",
